2 & & 0 & & 0 & \text{ (initially) } \\
2(1-x) & & 2 x & & x & \text{ (at equilibrium) }
\end{array} \begin{aligned} \text{Amount$ of $moles at equilibrium } & =2(1-x)+2 x+x \\ & =2+x\end{aligned}\)$\begin{aligned} & K_p= \frac{\left[p_{A B}\right]^2\left[p_{B_2}\right]$}{$\left[p_{A B_2}\right]^2}$ \\ & K_p= \frac{$\left(\frac{2 x}{2+x} \times$ P\right)^2$ \times$\left($\frac{x}{2+x} \times P\right)$}{$\left(\frac{2(1-x)}{2+x} \times$ P\right)^2$}=\frac{\frac{4 x^3}{2+x} \times P}{4(1-x)^2} \\ & K_p= \frac{4 x^3 \times P}{2} \times \frac{1}{4} \quad(\because 1-x \approx 1 \& 2+x \approx 2) \\ & x=$\left($\frac{8 K_p}{4 P}\right)^{1 / 3}$ \quad \Rightarrow x=$\left(\frac{2 K_p}{P}$\right)^{1 / 3}$\end{aligned}\)

